WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.038
SQL uses three-valued logic A condition can be TRUE
FALSE

00:00:06.235 --> 00:00:12.268
or UNKNOWN Comparing a normal value with NULL gives
UNKNOWN not FALSE

00:00:14.011 --> 00:00:19.544
And NOT UNKNOWN remains UNKNOWN Because WHERE
returns only rows whose

00:00:19.557 --> 00:00:25.468
condition is TRUE UNKNOWN behaves like a
filtered-out row This explains

00:00:25.494 --> 00:00:26.981
the NOT IN behavior
